From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: libretro's PresentWindow takes the GammaOS renderer's two new calls

The libretro core replaces the renderer's PresentWindow with its own
(citra_libretro/libretro_vk.h), which azahar-nano does not build. Its
renderer calls two methods it added to the swapchain one:
NotifySurfaceResized() (nothing to do here: the output texture follows each
frame) and RenderpassNoClear() (the present pass without the clear when the
first screen covers the frame; here the pass that clears, right for every
layout).

diff --git a/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.h b/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.h
index 5a60f75..92170ab 100644
--- a/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.h
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/libretro_vk.h
@@ -117,11 +117,19 @@ public:
 
     /// This is called to notify the rendering backend of a surface change
     void NotifySurfaceChanged();
+    /// The GammaOS renderer's swapchain resize: the output texture follows each frame here.
+    void NotifySurfaceResized() {}
 
     [[nodiscard]] vk::RenderPass Renderpass() const noexcept {
         return present_renderpass;
     }
 
+    /// The GammaOS renderer skips the clear when the first screen covers the frame; the
+    /// output pass here always clears, which is right for every layout.
+    [[nodiscard]] vk::RenderPass RenderpassNoClear() const noexcept {
+        return present_renderpass;
+    }
+
     u32 ImageCount() const noexcept {
         return static_cast<u32>(frame_pool.size());
     }
